[h1]The year is 1993. So is your user interface. All of it, in one mod.[/h1]
[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/11532297922866524150/0CE8390118378C79BB4D0A2400F1B010E55BE125/[/img]
[b]Dozens of pop-ups zapped into two.[/b] ZeD-GUI is a complete interface for Project Zomboid Build 42. Almost every window the game opens as a pop-up now lives in two windows: one for your [b]character[/b] and one for the [b]world[/b] around you. Both change with what's near you and what you can do.

[b]Perfected around the controller. Keyboard and mouse reap the rewards.[/b]

[h2]It won't break your game[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Safe mode.[/b] One switch gives you the game's own screens back, all of them or one at a time.
[*][b]Your mods still work.[/b] Context menu options, container buttons, items and recipes from other mods all show up. Buttons a mod adds inside the game's own inventory window don't.
[*][b]You're in control.[/b] The expanded mod options and the Safe mode switches let you tune it screen by screen, until it fits your mod list.
[*][b]Add or remove it any time.[/b] It adds one item, a digital watch, which leaves with the mod.
[*][b]Built to survive game updates.[/b] Official Lua only, nothing outside the game's own API.
[*][b]Same game underneath.[/b] ZeD changes how you see it, not how it plays.
[/list]

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Two windows that keep up with you.[/b] Walk up to a car and the Vehicle tab is there; leave and it goes. Health, skills, crafting, building, maps and foraging, all in one place.
[*][b]A card for every item,[/b] by the pointer as you loot.
[*][b]A HUD on a belt:[/b] your hands, your watch, a dashboard when you drive.
[*][b]A survival guide on F1[/b] with the game's live rules and numbers. F1 is your new Alt-Tab.
[*][b]Everything works on a controller,[/b] with buttons drawn for Xbox, PlayStation, Steam Deck or Nintendo.
[*][b]Access for all.[/b] Barriers removed or softened: high contrast, color blind status colors, two text sizes, text built to be read at a glance, wheels that need no held button. A commitment to every ability; tell us what still gets in your way.
[*][b]Your look:[/b] dark or light, nine accent colors, gadgets drawn as the real thing or as plain cards.
[/list]

[h2]Before you subscribe[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Build 42 only[/b] (tested on 42.21 and 42.22), at 4K, 1080p and on the Steam Deck.
[*][b]This is a beta.[/b] Use a new game or a copy of a save. The final release will be a separate item.
[*][b]English,[/b] with machine-drafted translations. Corrections welcome.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] every player needs it. Mod ID: ZeD_UI.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, then turn on [b]ZeD-GUI[/b] in Mods, after any other interface mods.
[*]Quit and start the game again, so its fonts load.
[*]Set it up in Options, ZeD setup.
[/olist]

[h2]Help and feedback[/h2]
Known issues, bug reports and translations each have a pinned discussion. To report a bug, open the ZeD wheel and pick [b]Bug report[/b]; it copies everything needed. Yell at me, tell me I'm pretty, party on.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Designed and directed by Hermit the Trog, built by Claude (see the discussion thread for more information). QA All-Star: FAIV. Fonts: Fira Sans, Fira Mono, Noto Sans SC (SIL Open Font License). Source-available on [url=https://github.com/hermit-the-trog/ZeD.UI]GitHub[/url]; please don't re-upload.

Project Zomboid is made by The Indie Stone. ZeD-GUI is a fan-made mod, not affiliated with The Indie Stone, Apple, Microsoft or Texas Instruments.
